# Migration Plan Phase 9: real, live-checked finding — Easy Auth blocks
# cross-origin CORS preflight before the BFF's own code ever runs, so
# the real, working shape is this app served SAME-ORIGIN by the BFF
# (see bff/main.py's own StaticFiles mount). Leave this UNSET for a real
# build (`npm run build`) meant to be served by the BFF — the client
# then uses relative fetches, resolving correctly against whatever
# origin actually serves it.
#
# Only set this to point `npm run dev` at a specific absolute origin for
# quick UI-only iteration on GET-driven views. POST calls (approve,
# reject, generate, chat) will still hit the same real Easy Auth
# preflight block when run this way — this is a real, disclosed
# limitation of local dev iteration, not a bug to chase.
# VITE_ONEPULSE_BFF_BASE_URL=https://onepulse-bff.wonderfulbay-b92b8b1b.centralus.azurecontainerapps.io
